# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Qwable-27B dense pair -- the CODEC-ONLY rows in bench/fair-battle.md and the 2026-09-03
# cross-engine table. Both are our own conversions of the Huihui Qwable-3.6-27B-abliterated
# F16 GGUF, quantized with this repo's llama-quantize per the "Quantizing your own model"
# section of docs/COOKBOOK.md; published at huggingface.co/poisonxa/Qwable-27B-GGUF.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PXQ4 core tier, 15,679,382,592 bytes. THIS is the benchmark file. A second, larger local
# build of the same tier exists (15,719,769,376 bytes, sha
# 4aabd929a308e24e10ee8eb1a6677cd5d97d0a4a715faf0a3889141a3eac19dc) -- it is NOT the file any
# published row was measured on; do not substitute it.
6fb4a437684e8bbedb2a34625fc4ade4137647bb85b7d2a6d9c4967d5452cb10  Qwable-27B-PXQ4core.gguf
# MXFP4 at matched bytes, 15,672,025,920 bytes: the codec-only control, and the single file the
# 2026-09-03 three-engine table runs on all three engines.
1d04b75817358cf7034fc9a5d3cc98a3aebfed5de60c9dbd831ab4771819960f  Qwable-27B-MXFP4-lite.gguf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 35B-A3B MoE pair -- the "MoE, 2xV100 (35B-A3B class)" expert-codec row in bench/fair-battle.md.
# Read that row as an expert-codec comparison, not a model comparison: the two sides are the
# same architecture and size class, not the same base weights (the caveat is stated in
# fair-battle.md itself).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The PXQ4 side: PXA-Fusion4-35B, our merge, quantized to PXQ4 with the MTP head.
# 19,296,360,576 bytes. Published at
# huggingface.co/poisonxa/PXA-Fusion4-35B-GGUF/PXA-Fusion4-35B-PXQ4.gguf -- the filename below
# is the published one. A second local build of the same tier exists under that same name
# (18,996,124,608 bytes, sha
# 35bdc0f7f86f41dbcaa24acc50f77cb65280c32d37065f3a21bb889b4edee792); it is NOT the file the
# MoE row was measured on. The sibling 2-bit tier in that repo is PXA-Fusion4-35B-PXQ2.gguf,
# sha 92d7c2533f034fc5548254d8f5a427456aec44c1160d95791e5221e985039fc5.
6fc30e1f9d3df634e6c97900ed04f5bd604b92786d351f72931120b00a814cf4  PXA-Fusion4-35B-PXQ4.gguf
# The MXFP4 side: the stock 35B-A3B model converted to MXFP4 with this repo's llama-quantize,
# 19,110,278,368 bytes. Published at
# huggingface.co/poisonxa/PXA-bench-files-GGUF/qwen36-35b-MXFP4.gguf. Referenced by exactly one
# published row -- the "MoE, 2xV100 (35B-A3B class)" table in bench/fair-battle.md.
5fc152ba23f958ef681b92279c52b49817b3f5eafd04e0a0a3ba0824467977cf  qwen36-35b-MXFP4.gguf

